Why the Hybrid Approach is the Winner

In Years 1 through 3, you executed an aggressive "bracket bumping" strategy by converting massive amounts (~$230k/year) to build your seasoned Roth ladder. That was a great move.
But by Year 8, the mission changes. You have already won the ladder game—you successfully built a huge, tax-sheltered pool of seasoned money. Forcing another massive $141k conversion in Year 8 means you are needlessly paying high taxes to feed a ladder you no longer need to overfund, especially since your 401(k) balance is winding down to $790k.
Dropping your conversions and coasting on a small SEPP combined with tax-free Roth withdrawals lets you keep thousands of dollars in your pocket instead of giving it to the IRS.
